// synth: library theory (phase 0)
// doc: Models Python's range(start, end) with step +1 and integer arguments.
// doc: For integers start and end, Python's range(start, end) yields the
// doc: sequence of integers start, start+1, ..., end-1. If start >= end the
// doc: sequence is empty. Python accepts arbitrarily large integers (no
// doc: overflow), and if non-integer arguments are supplied Python would raise
// doc: a TypeError; this Dafny function assumes integer arguments and thus
// doc: models only the integer-to-integer case. No exceptions are raised by
// doc: this function for integer inputs.
// doc: This function is total on Dafny's int type and is implemented
// doc: recursively; it decreases by end - start to ensure termination.
function Range(start: int, end: int): seq<int>
  decreases end - start
{
  if start >= end then
    []
  else
    [start] + Range(start + 1, end)
}

