// doc: Python's % (modulo) operator for integers returns the remainder r of the
// doc: Euclidean division a = b*q + r, chosen so that r has the sign of the
// doc: divisor b (i.e., 0 <= r < b when b > 0, and b <= r <= 0 when b < 0).
// doc: When b == 0, Python raises a ZeroDivisionError; to model this we make
// doc: this function partial with the precondition b != 0. For all integers a
